{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"busy-mirky-borer","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe tests/unit cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `tests/unit/test_det_measurement_provenance_heldout.py:1-8` — Preserve the measurement-provenance regression boundary. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_detached_child_cwd.py:1-19, 111-116` — Preserve detached-child working-directory independence. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_divergence_grade_split.py:1-16, 145-149` — Preserve the distinction between divergence grades. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_doctor_dirty_tree.py:1-22` — Preserve doctor diagnostics for a dirty ticket-store tree. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_doctor_mapping.py:1-19, 543-561` — Preserve doctor issue-to-remediation mapping and output contract. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_doctor_mcp_client.py:1-19` — Preserve MCP-client doctor checks and actionable diagnostics. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_engine_dir.py:152-176` — Preserve engine-directory resolution and isolation invariants. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_enrich_drain.py:61-66, 189-205, 472-480, 714-719, 1048-1059, 1177-1182` — Preserve drain ordering, retry, failure, and concurrency invariants. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_enrich_queue.py:201-204, 341-347, 502-510, 526-533, 606-613, 667-675` — Preserve queue deduplication, persistence, ordering, and error contracts. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_ensures_boot_budget_e43f.py:1-14` — Preserve the ensure-registry boot-time budget invariant. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_ensures_late_binding_isolation.py:1-20` — Preserve isolation between late-bound ensure implementations. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_ensures_late_binding.py:1-19, 38-53` — Preserve late binding of ensure implementations and the tested seam. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_env_registry_helper_coverage.py:1-17, 87-96, 130-139` — Preserve environment-registry helper coverage and ownership boundaries. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_epic_bug_screen_4b54.py:1-29, 525-533` — Preserve epic bug-screen classification and false-positive boundaries. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_error_code_insecure_url_7d6a.py:1-10` — Preserve the stable error code for insecure URLs. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_error_handling_convention.py:1-12` — Preserve the repository error-handling convention contract. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_eval_scorers.py:229-239, 250-254` — Preserve scoring edge cases and calibration semantics. Consumer: test maintainers.\n- `tests/unit/test_eval_solver_project_criterion.py:1-12` — Preserve project-criterion evaluation behavior. Consumer: test maintainers.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every preserve item and consumer contract in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by a row-by-row completion comment and the commands under Verification.\n- [ ] No executable behavior or test assertion changes; verified by the commands under Verification exiting 0.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" pytest tests/unit/test_det_measurement_provenance_heldout.py tests/unit/test_detached_child_cwd.py tests/unit/test_divergence_grade_split.py tests/unit/test_doctor_dirty_tree.py tests/unit/test_doctor_mapping.py tests/unit/test_doctor_mcp_client.py tests/unit/test_engine_dir.py tests/unit/test_enrich_drain.py tests/unit/test_enrich_queue.py tests/unit/test_ensures_boot_budget_e43f.py tests/unit/test_ensures_late_binding_isolation.py tests/unit/test_ensures_late_binding.py tests/unit/test_env_registry_helper_coverage.py tests/unit/test_epic_bug_screen_4b54.py tests/unit/test_error_code_insecure_url_7d6a.py tests/unit/test_error_handling_convention.py tests/unit/test_eval_scorers.py tests/unit/test_eval_solver_project_criterion.py`\n\nThe row-by-row diff review is authoritative for prose quality; the hygiene guard detects only its narrow deterministic history-token rule.","id":"029a-c2e8-b4af-44db","parent_id":"ae4d-df34-480d-4c88","priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Condense comments in tests/unit — cohort 10: det_measurement_provenance_heldout–eval_solver_project_criterion"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788571407645325619,"uuid":"be5665f1-4e89-4366-b6f9-6715fe52efbd"}